    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31055" root="عوق" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيِّقٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيَّقٌ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُوَقٌ</span>, first signification. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
It is also used as an imitative sequent: one says
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَيِّقٌ لَيِّقٌ عَيِّقٌ</span> (K) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَيِّقٌ عَيِّقٌ لَيِّقٌ</span> (IAar, TA)
[app. meaning <i>Very niggardly</i>]: or, as some say,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَيِّقٌ</span> signifies as expl. voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُوَقٌ</span>, and is not an
imitative sequent. (TA.)

